SUMMARY:An Afternoon with Carrie Simon!
LOCATION:Cavalier House Books\, 302A Jefferson St
DESCRIPTION:Join us at CHB Lafayette on Nov. 21 at 3 p.m. for a Q+A and boo
 k signing with Carrie Simon!\nCarrie will discuss her latest book\, The Gi
 rl Who Ate Flowers\, in a moderated Q&A led by Rachel Comeaux Lanclos. The
  Girl Who Ate Flowers is a story of the quiet town of Harvey\, Louisiana\,
  when it was shattered by the disappearance and murder of twelve-year-old 
 Susanne Lee. Years later\, the case remains unsolved when an unrelenting i
 nvestigative journalist from The Manhattan Times\, arrives determined to u
 ncover the truth. But in Harvey\, asking questions can be dangerous-and th
 ose who dig too deep don't always make it out. Haunting\, atmospheric\, an
 d impossible to put down\, *The Girl Who Ate Flowers* is a psychological t
 hriller that grips readers to the final page-and just as the truth begins 
 to surface\, a shocking revelation suggests that Susanne's death is only t
 he beginning.\nRSVP for this afternoon with Carrie Simon through Bon Temps
  Tix! Books will be available at the event!\n\nhttps://www.downtownlafayet
 te.org/event/an-afternoon-with-carrie-simon
